			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2237959">
									

<p>I think that was actually the most jarring of the article for me. I know you didn't come up with the GoI's name, but normally occultist (or even religious) group names in Chinese would end with something like &quot;Jiao&quot; (Cult/Religion), &quot;Zong&quot; (Sect) or &quot;Dafa&quot; (Great Way), and the particle &quot;de&quot; as an adjective indicator would always be omitted, and as a possessive would be replaced by the more archaic &quot;zhi&quot;.</p>
<p>Also, the proper pinyin is H<strong>uo</strong>ju.</p>

